# proofs/MUTANTS: one-token mutants (GOAL.md §2.4). tools/mutate.py applies each to a scratch copy of the overlay.
# card= names the card whose proofs must kill it: UB-relevant mutants belong to the P1 card of their function,
# functional ones (no UB, wrong value) to the P2/P3 card. A mutant is killed only when a proof of its own card fails
# (checkpoint 1, D1): another card's failing proof is reported and does not count.
# Format: M-NNN <function> <upstream line> '<from>' '<to>' card=C-NN [equivalent='<argument>' review=<file>]
# M-001 to M-016 are the pilot set (bring-up); M-017 to M-062 complete it at checkpoint 1 (GOAL.md §2.4), at least two
# per Appendix A function; M-063 to M-065 come from the checkpoint 1 audit (fix 6). While a card has no proofs here
# or on main, its mutants are PENDING (not run); `make gate ALLOW_PENDING=1` passes them, and plain `make gate`,
# the §5 gate, fails on any (tools/mutate.py).
# Expected equivalent: none. Every mutant below is either UB the frozen checks catch on any proof of the function
# (out-of-footprint reads and writes, undefined shifts, signed overflow, division by zero, a float-to-int conversion
# out of range, a loop that never ends), or a wrong value that P2 or P3 compares. Four kills also need what a
# card's notes say its contract must state, because a caller relies on it:
#   M-046, M-047 (C-13): sqlite3VdbeMemSetNull ensures pMem->flags == MEM_Null; RecordUnpack calls it for that (92150).
#   M-048, M-049 (C-14): AllocUnpackedRecord ensures p->aMem holds p->nField writable Mems; RecordUnpack needs that.
#   M-057, M-058 (C-18): sqlite3VdbeRecordCompare's call meets WithSkip's requires for bSkip == 0 and for pKey1 only.
#   M-061 (C-20): A-001's slack is the smallest that works, so a header offset up to 0x7F plus 8 bytes exceeds it.
#
# putVarint64 (37967): writes past the 9-byte footprint, or a loop that never ends.
M-001 putVarint64 37971 'p[8]' 'p[9]' card=C-01
M-002 putVarint64 37973 'i--' 'i++' card=C-01
M-003 putVarint64 37982 'v >>= 7' 'v >>= 6' card=C-01
# putVarint64: wrong encoding, no UB (killed by the P2 round trip).
M-004 putVarint64 37970 '<<32' '<<33' card=C-02
M-005 putVarint64 37974 '0x7f' '0x3f' card=C-02
# sqlite3PutVarint (37991): writes past the footprint.
M-006 sqlite3PutVarint 37998 'p[1]' 'p[9]' card=C-01
M-007 sqlite3PutVarint 37993 'p[0]' 'p[9]' card=C-01
# sqlite3PutVarint: wrong encoding.
M-008 sqlite3PutVarint 37992 '0x7f' '0xff' card=C-02
M-009 sqlite3PutVarint 37996 '0x3fff' '0x7fff' card=C-02
